# v2 entrypoint — dramatiq replaces celery.
# --processes 1 always: Demucs/librosa analysis is memory-heavy. Threads stay
# at 1 HERE because this single all-queues dev entry runs batch DSP; the
# interactive pool (`coach ai` — I/O-bound LLM actors) is the one that runs
# several threads (scripts/start-spectr.ps1, infra/compose.prod.yml
# WORKER_THREADS). The LLM gateway builds a fresh client per call and keeps
# its semaphores thread-local, so multi-threading that pool is safe.
#
# Queues (AR23, story 2.5 + interactive AI lane): one dev worker drains ALL
# five queues, so every message gets processed by one process. The pool
# split lives in scripts/start-spectr.ps1 (dev) / infra/compose.prod.yml.
#   ai            : run_triage, run_specialist, generate_fix_rack (interactive LLM)
#   ai-guest      : the same three actors, enqueued for demo guests (own pool in prod)
#   analysis-paid : pro/credits analysis + batch auxiliaries (rerun_phase,
#                   run_reference_analyzer, classify_stems, detect_structure_job)
#   analysis-free : free/anon analysis (sole declarer = analyze_audio_job)
#   coach         : coach_reply
#   maintenance   : sweep_retention (story 3.4), send_email, delete_account_data
# `default` is dropped — no producer remains after story 2.5. If you run against
# a long-lived dev Redis that may hold stray `default` messages, append `default`.
worker: python -m dramatiq app.dramatiq_app --processes 1 --threads 1 --queues coach ai ai-guest analysis-paid analysis-free maintenance
